<Vertical id="ChatWithSidebar" title="Interactive Discussion">

<Markdown>
# Legacy code / deprecated syntax

We originally repointed the sidebar with:
```
sidebar -> follow_up_activity
```
Which just sets the field. Setting a field is useful, so we are continuing to support arrow syntax (although we might flip the arrow or left/right sides -- the current version is a bit counterintuitive).

We now have dedicated syntax for embedding activities which supercedes this:

```
::prediction [display=target:sidebar]
```

Legacy content should be migrated, but this is not urgent as setting a field still technically works, even if it is not semantic.

This might continue to evolve. We would like this to be /more/ semantic.
</Markdown>

  <!-- Activities that appear in the sidebar -->
  <Hidden>
    <Markdown id="sidebar_intro">Activities will appear here as the conversation progresses.</Markdown>
    <Vertical id="initial_thoughts_activity">
      <Markdown>**What do you already know about effective study techniques?**</Markdown>
      <TextArea id="initial_thoughts" placeholder="Type your thoughts here..." />
      <ActionButton id="submit_initial" dependsOn="initial_thoughts" target="interactive_chat" action="advance" label="Submit" />
    </Vertical>
    <Vertical id="follow_up_activity">
      <Markdown>**How might you apply these strategies to your own studying?**</Markdown>
      <TextArea id="follow_up" placeholder="Describe your plan..." />
      <ActionButton id="submit_follow_up" dependsOn="follow_up" target="interactive_chat" action="advance" label="Submit" />
    </Vertical>
    <Vertical id="spacing_goal_activity">
      <Markdown>**Set a spaced-practice goal:** How many shorter sessions will you spread across this week? Aim for at least 3.</Markdown>
      <NumberInput id="spacing_goal" placeholder="e.g., 4" />
      <ActionButton id="submit_spacing_goal" dependsOn="spacing_goal" target="interactive_chat" action="advance" label="Save goal" />
    </Vertical>
    <Vertical id="confidence_check_activity">
      <Markdown>**Confidence check (0-1):** Rate how confident you are about sticking with spaced practice and add one thing that would boost it.</Markdown>
      <NumberInput id="confidence_score" min="0" max="1" step="0.1" placeholder="e.g., 0.8" />
      <TextArea id="confidence_note" placeholder="What's one thing that could raise it?" />
      <ActionButton id="submit_confidence" dependsOn="confidence_score, confidence_note" target="interactive_chat" action="advance" label="Share confidence" />
    </Vertical>
  </Hidden>

  <SplitPanel sizes="65,35">
    <LeftPane>
      <Chat id="interactive_chat" title="Study Session">
title: Study Session
~~~~

Alex: Welcome! Before we dive in - what do you already know about study techniques?

--- wait initial_thoughts ---

Alex: Thanks for sharing! Here's what research tells us.

Alex: Active recall - testing yourself - is far more effective than passive review like re-reading.

Sam: Like using flashcards?

Alex: Exactly! And spacing practice over time beats cramming.

responseSidebar -> follow_up_activity

Alex: Now, how might you apply this?

--- wait follow_up ---

Alex: Great plan! The key is making it a habit.

responseSidebar -> spacing_goal_activity

Alex: Let's set a quick spaced-practice goal. Enter how many short sessions you'll spread across this week.

--- wait spacing_goal value>=3 ---

Alex: Planning at least three sessions is a solid start.

responseSidebar -> confidence_check_activity

Alex: Finally, rate your confidence in sticking with the plan and note one thing that would make it even easier.

--- wait confidence_score value>=0.7, confidence_note ---

Alex: Awesome—feeling 0.7 or higher and having a booster plan means you're ready to try this.

Sam: Thanks for the tips!
      </Chat>
    </LeftPane>
    <RightPane>
      <Markdown>### Your Responses</Markdown>
      <UseHistory id="responseSidebar" initial="initial_thoughts_activity" />
    </RightPane>
  </SplitPanel>

